  "title": "Appleseed Audiobook MEG",
  "description": "This dataset contains magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from 12 participants listening to continuous narrative speech, along with an empty-room recording, stimulus files, and derivatives. The study investigates how listeners integrate local and unified predictive models during speech perception, examining neural signatures of contextual prediction at phoneme and sentence levels. Source localization analyses implicate bilateral superior temporal regions in these parallel predictive processes.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were recorded from 12 subjects listening to continuous narrative speech, with an accompanying empty-room recording. Data are stored in FIFF format and were processed using MNE-Python. MRI data were derived from the fsaverage template using subject-specific scaling parameters rather than individual anatomical scans.",
